---Describes the properties of an agreement.
---@class aws.transfer.DescribedAgreement
---@field Arn aws.transfer.Arn The unique Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the agreement.
---@field AgreementId? aws.transfer.AgreementId A unique identifier for the agreement. This identifier is returned when you create an agreement.
---@field Description? aws.transfer.Description The name or short description that's used to identify the agreement.
---@field Status? aws.transfer.AgreementStatusType The current status of the agreement, either ACTIVE or INACTIVE.
---@field ServerId? aws.transfer.ServerId A system-assigned unique identifier for a server instance. This identifier indicates the specific server that the agreement uses.
---@field LocalProfileId? aws.transfer.ProfileId A unique identifier for the AS2 local profile.
---@field PartnerProfileId? aws.transfer.ProfileId A unique identifier for the partner profile used in the agreement.
---@field BaseDirectory? aws.transfer.HomeDirectory The landing directory (folder) for files that are transferred by using the AS2 protocol.
---@field AccessRole? aws.transfer.Role Connectors are used to send files using either the AS2 or SFTP protocol. For the access role, provide the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Identity and Access Management role to use.
