---@field Usage? aws.transfer.CertificateUsageType Specifies how this certificate is used. It can be used in the following ways:
---@field Status? aws.transfer.CertificateStatusType A certificate's status can be either ACTIVE or INACTIVE.
---@field Certificate? distilled.Secret The file name for the certificate.
---@field CertificateChain? distilled.Secret The list of certificates that make up the chain for the certificate.
---@field ActiveDate? aws.transfer.CertDate An optional date that specifies when the certificate becomes active. If you do not specify a value, ActiveDate takes the same value as NotBeforeDate, which is specified by the CA.
---@field InactiveDate? aws.transfer.CertDate An optional date that specifies when the certificate becomes inactive. If you do not specify a value, InactiveDate takes the same value as NotAfterDate, which is specified by the CA.
---@field Serial? aws.transfer.CertSerial The serial number for the certificate.
---@field NotBeforeDate? aws.transfer.CertDate The earliest date that the certificate is valid.
---@field NotAfterDate? aws.transfer.CertDate The final date that the certificate is valid.
---@field Type? aws.transfer.CertificateType If a private key has been specified for the certificate, its type is CERTIFICATE_WITH_PRIVATE_KEY. If there is no private key, the type is CERTIFICATE.
---@field Description? aws.transfer.Description The name or description that's used to identity the certificate.
---@field Tags? aws.transfer.Tags Key-value pairs that can be used to group and search for certificates.

---Describes the parameters for the connector, as identified by the ConnectorId.
---@class aws.transfer.DescribedConnector
---@field Arn aws.transfer.Arn The unique Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the connector.
